---
import ChecklistPage from '../components/ChecklistPage.astro';
import { checklist, totalChecks } from '../data/seo-audit-checklist';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is an SEO audit?',
    a: 'An SEO audit is a health check of a website. It looks at whether search engines can crawl and index the pages, whether each page matches a real search, how fast the site loads, and what is holding rankings back.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How often should I run an SEO audit?',
    a: 'A full audit once or twice a year is enough for most small sites. Run one again after a redesign, a move to a new platform, or a sudden drop in traffic. The tracking checks are worth a look every month.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which tools do I need for this checklist?',
    a: 'Google Search Console and PageSpeed Insights cover most of it, and both are free. The Rich Results Test checks structured data. A crawler such as Screaming Frog helps on larger sites.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is my score saved?',
    a: 'Your ticks are saved in your own browser only. Nothing is sent anywhere, and clearing your browser data removes them.',
  },
];

// Official Google tools only, so the links stay stable and neutral.
const tools = [
  { name: 'Google Search Console', href: 'https://search.google.com/search-console', use: 'Indexing, sitemaps, and which searches show your pages.' },
  { name: 'PageSpeed Insights', href: 'https://pagespeed.web.dev/', use: 'Core Web Vitals and what slows a page down.' },
  { name: 'Rich Results Test', href: 'https://search.google.com/test/rich-results', use: 'Checks structured data for errors.' },
  { name: 'Google Business Profile', href: 'https://www.google.com/business/', use: 'Your listing on Maps and in local results.' },
];
---

<ChecklistPage
  path="/seo-audit-checklist.html"
  title={`SEO Audit Checklist: ${totalChecks} Checks You Can Tick Off`}
  description={`A free SEO audit checklist with ${totalChecks} checks across crawling, on-page SEO, speed, structured data, AI answers, and local search. Tick them off and see your score.`}
  name="SEO audit checklist"
  h1="SEO audit checklist"
  lead={`An SEO audit checklist is a list of the things to check when a website is not getting the search traffic it should. This one has ${totalChecks} checks in ${checklist.length} groups. Tick what is already done and the score shows where to look next.`}
  how="Work from the top. The groups are in order of importance, so a gap in the first group matters more than a gap in the last. This is a self-check, not a full audit: it tells you where to look, not everything that is wrong."
  groups={checklist}
  storageKey="seo-audit-checklist-v1"
  faqs={faqs}
  tools={tools}
  toolsIntro="All from Google, all free. Between them they cover most of this list."
  nextHeading="Want this checked properly?"
  nextCta="Ask for an audit"
>
  A checklist shows where to look. A full audit crawls every page, reads the Search
  Console data, and gives you the fixes in order. Read
  <a href="/blog/technical-seo-audit-checklist-2026.html">the longer technical audit guide</a>,
  try the <a href="/aeo-checklist.html">AEO checklist</a> and the
  <a href="/geo-checklist.html">GEO checklist</a>, or see
  <a href="/services/seo.html">how I do SEO</a>.
</ChecklistPage>
